# Line endings: the repository stores LF, working trees get native endings.
#
# Added 09 Sep 2026. pom.xml had been committed with CRLF, so git saw it as a
# whole-file rewrite against every other branch: a merge that really touched
# ~68 lines would have conflicted on all 2622. This pins the convention so it
# cannot recur on anyone's machine regardless of their core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto

# Binary assets, never convert.
*.jar   binary
*.gz    binary
*.z     binary
*.xls   binary
*.ods   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.png   binary
*.pfx   binary
*.p12   binary
*.class binary

# The vendored SUT clones (jsoup, ta4j, threeten-extra) ship their own
# .gitattributes, which take precedence for their subtrees. Their binary and
# encoded test fixtures are already covered there; nothing extra is needed here.
